  "final_output": "## Root cause\nThe Order v3.4.0 deploy at 10:48 UTC (\"Structured shipping address for pickup points\") broke the Delivery consumer. The new Order pods publish order.paid with schema_version=2. In this version shipping_address is an object, not a string. The Delivery consumer cannot parse it. It fails on offset 1854162 (order ord_V6WMXG) and retries the same message again and again. It has no DLQ for parse errors, so it never moves on. It books no shipment for any order paid after the deploy.\n\n## Evidence\n- list_changes 10:00 to 12:00: Order v3.4.0 deploy at 10:48. The cart v2.1.0 deploy at 09:40 is 68 minutes before the first error and is not on the order.paid path.\n- search_logs for delivery errors: \"failed to process message, will retry\" for offset 1854162, schema_version=2, with the error \"cannot unmarshal object into Go struct field OrderPaid.shipping_address of type string\". The first error is at 10:48:19, 19 seconds after the deploy, and the attempt count grows.\n- query_metric kafka_consumer_lag{group=delivery}: about 0 to 1 until 10:46, then 23 at 10:48, 119 at 10:52, and 2045 at 11:59. It never drains. kafka_lag shows the groups order (max 6) and notification (max 9) are normal. The alert fired at 11:33 when lag passed 1000.\n- get_order_timeline ord_V6WMXG: paid at 10:48:18, event published: order.paid, then only the order_confirmed email. There is no carrier booking step.\n- third_party_health carrier 10:00 to 12:00: booking requests have an average of 15 per minute (normal 24), and the last value is 3. Calls were about 29 per minute in the hour before the deploy and are about 5 per minute from 10:49. This shows that Delivery sends no booking. The carrier error rate averages 0.1% and latency is normal (p95 about 680 ms). The carrier is healthy. The ThirdPartyErrors alert at 01:05 was the nightly maintenance window and it resolved at 01:15.\n- business_kpis 10:00 to 12:00: checkout success 96.7% and payment success are normal. Only 1 order is stuck pending, below the alert limit of 5.\n- list_alerts and dlq_sample: DlqGrowing for group notification is about order_shipped emails to deleted mailboxes (550 mailbox does not exist). The delivery group has no DLQ messages. This is a known issue and it is not related.\n\n## Customer impact\nSince 10:49 UTC (about 70 minutes) no paid order gets a carrier booking, and carrier booking calls fall from about 29 to about 5 per minute. About 2,045 paid orders wait in the order.paid topic at 12:00, and the number grows by about 30 for each minute. Customers are charged and get the confirmation email, but their orders do not ship and they get no tracking. Checkout, payment and emails work. The fault is still active.\n\n## Next steps\n1. Roll back Order from v3.4.0 to v3.3.2 now. This stops new v2 events.\n2. Ship a Delivery consumer that reads schema v2 (or add a converter). The v2 messages that are already in the topic need it.\n3. Let Delivery process the backlog. Do not skip or delete the messages, or the orders never ship. Check that the lag for group delivery falls to 0 and that carrier booking calls return to the normal level (about 24 per minute).\n4. Later: add a DLQ for parse errors, a schema compatibility check in CI, and an alert when a consumer makes no progress."
